/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  thermoPhysPropDict (v2) -- gamma-phi, ideal liquid (gamma = 1, DECLARED),
  SRK vapour.

  The column runs at 16 bar.  There the vapour is not ideal: the 2026-11-07
  audit (C239) measured phi of the light key about 21 % below 1, so an
  ideal-gas vapour misprices both K and the latent heats.  The vapour is
  therefore SRK (kij = 0, announced -- hydrocarbon pairs, no interaction
  data declared).  The pure-liquid reference carries phi_sat and Poynting.
  The MESH iterates visit temperatures above the critical temperature of
  propane (369.8 K) and butane (425.1 K), where a saturated vapour does not
  exist: the reference factor is HELD at its value at 0.99 Tc (continuous
  in T, announced once per component) instead of jumping to 1.

  No interior seed is declared (since 2026-11-08, DEV.md 4c C245 slice 4).
  Until then the column started from a stage profile declared in 0/,
  because from the built-in linear start the CMO phase that seeds the full
  MESH converged (|F| 2.6e-14) to a TRIVIAL profile: T 287-300 K, x = y on
  every stage.  A stage vapour at 287 K and 16 bar has ONE cubic root, a
  liquid-like one, and SRK handed it to the vapour too: both phases on one
  root, every K about 1.  The cubic now returns a flagged PSEUDO-ROOT for a
  phase that has no root of its own (CubicEoS.H), and from the linear
  start the CMO phase converges in 14 Newton iterations to the real
  profile and the full MESH in 4 -- the same answer the seed gave.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components       ( propane  nButane  nPentane  nHexane );

equilibrium
{
    formulation gammaPhi;

    liquid
    {
        activityModel ideal;
        standardState pureLiquid;
    }

    vapour
    {
        fugacityModel SRK;
    }
}
